### VietPay — Wallet flows (wallet-service via Traefik, JWT-protected)
### Run `login` first; wallet calls read the token inline via
### {{login.response.body.accessToken}}. (IntelliJ: use ...body.$.accessToken)

@baseUrl = http://localhost
@email = dajneem234@yopmail.com
@password = Password123!
@adminEmail = admin@vietpay.com
@adminPassword = Admin123!


### Login to obtain an access token
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Create a wallet (USD) -> 201
# @name createWallet
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/wallets
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currency": "USD"
}

### List all my wallets -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/wallets
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Get the wallet balance -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/wallets/{{createWallet.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Login as ADMIN (deposit requires ADMIN role, gated at wallet-service)
# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

### Deposit $100 into the wallet (ADMIN-only; safe to retry via Idempotency-Key) -> 201
# POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/wallets/{{createWallet.response.body.id}}/deposits
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/wallets/b9f4ab7c-2bb1-4e19-935e-a2de4f477265/deposits
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Idempotency-Key: dep-53111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": "100.00",
  "currency": "USD"
}

### Retry the SAME deposit (same key) -> credited once (idempotent replay)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/wallets/{{createWallet.response.body.id}}/deposits
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Idempotency-Key: dep-11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": "100.00",
  "currency": "USD"
}

### Non-admin user tried deposit -> 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/wallets/{{createWallet.response.body.id}}/deposits
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Idempotency-Key: dep-22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": "1.00",
  "currency": "USD"
}

### Balance after deposit -> 100.00
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/wallets/{{createWallet.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}


### Unsupported currency -> 422 (valid ISO but not offered)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/wallets
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currency": "KWD"
}

### Malformed currency -> 400 (not a real ISO code)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/wallets
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currency": "US"
}

### Unknown wallet -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/wallets/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000009
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### No token -> 401 (Traefik ForwardAuth rejects before wallet-service)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/wallets/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000009



### get reconciliation for a wallet -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/wallets/{{createWallet.response.body.id}}/reconciliation
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}


### ---- Transfer ----------------------------------------------------------
### Uses `createWallet` (funded by the deposit above) as the source, so this
### now succeeds. Demonstrates the Idempotency-Key header + idempotent retry.

### Create a destination wallet -> 201
# @name destWallet
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/wallets
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currency": "USD"
}

### Transfer $10.00 with an idempotency key
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Idempotency-Key: 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceWalletId": "{{createWallet.response.body.id}}",
  "destWalletId": "{{destWallet.response.body.id}}",
  "amount": "10.00",
  "currency": "USD"
}

### Retry the SAME request with the SAME key -> money moves once (idempotent replay)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Idempotency-Key: 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceWalletId": "{{createWallet.response.body.id}}",
  "destWalletId": "{{destWallet.response.body.id}}",
  "amount": "10.00",
  "currency": "USD"
}

### Source wallet transaction history (shows the debit) -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/wallets/{{createWallet.response.body.id}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

